  "body": "Stacked on #4249. This PR contains the commits of #4249. Merge #4249 first; then this PR takes `git merge origin/main` and a new gate. Do not merge this PR before #4249.\n\nThe own commit of this PR is `22517a3f5` (on top of #4249 head `3ab6f4ae3`).\n\n## What changed\n\nA turning tool can now be assembled from linked document components (holder + turning insert) through the document commands, as a milling tool can.\n\n- `crates/app/src/tool_assembly.rs` `derive` sends a lathe-held stack to the new submodule `tool_assembly_lathe.rs`. That module calls `camcraft_tools::lathe_assembly::resolve_lathe` (#4194).\n- The commands `SetToolAssembly`, `EditDocumentComponent` and `UpsertDocumentComponent` land these in one undo step:\n  - the Turning record: the nose radius, the orientation (`None` for the default 2), the insert's inscribed circle as `diameter`, and the insert row's running data;\n  - the lathe-frame `ToolBody`, built with `tool_body_lathe::build` from the resolver's placement and placed facets.\n- An edit of the shared insert updates each tool that uses it in one undo step. Their operations go Stale by their stamps.\n- `DocumentComponent` gets `lathe_body: Option<LatheBody>`. `EditDocumentComponent::new` keeps it.\n- `camcraft_tools::lathe_assembly::ResolvedLathe` gets `placed`, the facets that its bands were read from. This is an additive field.\n- These are refused by name, and nothing changes:\n  - a grooving, threading or form tool stack;\n  - a root that is not a rectangular shank or a round (or Weldon) shank, for example a VDI block;\n  - each refusal of the lathe resolver;\n  - a row with a lathe body in a spindle stack. A body is never dropped in silence.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/3643-lathe-app-caller.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/lathe_stack.rs` (a module of the `tool_library_holders` suite, no new top-level binary):\n\n- `a_linked_cnmg_in_a_pclnr_equals_the_tools_crate_result`: the equivalence pin. A CNMG120408 in a PCLNR2525M12 from document rows gives the same Turning record and the same placement, bands and facets as `resolve_lathe` on the same components.\n- `one_shared_turning_insert_edit_updates_two_holders_in_one_undo_step`: CNMG120408 to CNMG120404 updates a PCLNR2525M12 tool and a PCLNR2020K12 tool. Both Facing operations go Stale. Undo and redo are exact.\n- `a_kind_a_root_or_a_stack_the_lathe_resolver_does_not_take_is_refused_by_name`: a grooving tool, a VDI root, a wrong-hand holder and an end mill on a lathe body are refused by name, and no tool gets a stack or a body.\n\n## Gate (Mac, lane 2, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`, head `22517a3f5fbe33152036754542dbfae7b892ecd6`)\n\nThe log has the head SHA on its first line: `gate-3643c-22517a3f5fbe33152036754542dbfae7b892ecd6.log`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base 3ab6f4ae3fe36ca1eec3db77875b02064553422f`: 43 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes `tools suites: lib` and `app suites: tool_library_holders`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- Pinning tests: 3 passed.\n- No heavy step (P6). No post or toolpath generator changed, so no example catalog suite was run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The project file does not save the component table yet. #4233 (#3645) owns `crates/app/src/project/` and must write and read `lathe_body` with the other row fields.\n- There is no MCP tool and no UI for a lathe body on a row. `crates/app/src/mcp/` (#4268) and `crates/ui/` (#4271) are in other open PRs. They call the same commands.\n- A boring bar in a sleeve (a VDI root) is refused by name. Its station is a separate open item of #3643.\n\nStill open on #3643: STEP/STL/OBJ mesh bodies, `MCS_INSERT` as `CsysRole::Mounting` in `step_csys.rs`, and the boring-bar overhang in a sleeve.\n\nChangelog: A turning tool can be assembled from a shared holder and insert in the document. An edit of the insert updates each tool that uses it in one undo step.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #3643\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
